<Base title="Nationals slots" description="How the Alabama Section earns USPSA National Championship slots and how they are distributed.">
  <PageHead title="Nationals slots" lede="Every year USPSA awards each Section a number of invitations (&quot;slots&quot;) to the USPSA National Championships. The Section decides who gets them. Here is how that works in Alabama." />
  <div class="container">

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How the Section earns slots</h2>
      <p>Activity fees paid to USPSA by every Alabama club are pooled into a single Section-wide count (Bylaws Art. 9). USPSA converts that activity into slots for the Section under its <a href="https://uspsa.org/policies/Nationals-Policies" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Nationals Slot Policy</a>, roughly one slot per ten participants per division, capped per division. More shooters at Alabama club matches means more slots for Alabama.</p>
      <p>Slots earned through performance at the previous Nationals or at the Area 6 Championship go directly to the shooter and do not pass through the Section.</p>

      <h2>How the Section distributes them</h2>
      <p>USPSA policy requires that a Section's distribution method <em>always</em> considers placement in matches, <em>may</em> also consider club membership and assistance at events, and <em>never</em> awards slots by lottery or random selection (Section Operations and Governance Policy §2.5(c)-(d)).</p>
      <p><strong>For 2027, slots are awarded by application.</strong> Shooters who want a Section slot apply to the Section Coordinator; applications are evaluated on match placement first, with club membership and help at Section events also considered. Slots previously distributed by drawing did not meet USPSA policy, and the Section has corrected that.</p>
      <p>The 2019 bylaws (Art. 11) still describe the old method and will be amended by the Executive Committee to match. Until then, the process on this page controls.</p>

      <h2>How to apply</h2>
      <p>Application details for 2027 (window, what to include, where to send it) will be posted under <a href="/notices/">Notices</a> once USPSA publishes the Section's allocation. <span class="soon">Coming soon</span></p>

      <h2>2027 allocation</h2>
      <p>Posted once slots have been awarded. <span class="soon">Coming soon</span></p>
